<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Quantity strings.

    THE RULE, learned the hard way: a plural resource holds the WHOLE PHRASE,
    never just the counted noun. English lets you get away with wrapping one
    word because the verb does not agree - "1 tick will write" / "5 ticks will
    write". Ukrainian agrees the verb, and pulling it out of the plural
    produces "21 позначка створять", which is wrong in a way an English
    speaker never has to think about.

    THE LIMIT: an Android plural takes ONE quantity. A sentence whose two
    numbers vary independently ("2 ticks will write 2 records") cannot be one
    resource - it has to be composed from two, or reworded so only one number
    is inflected. Every string below is worded to need exactly one.
-->
